1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Fullsend Auto-Merge runs for real in a private lab—not as a forge button or observe-only mock.

2
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:30,000
The decision binds one repository, pull request, exact head, live base, policy, and evidence context.

3
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:45,000
Review and a fast CI contract check begin independently.

4
00:00:45,000 --> 00:01:00,000
A deliberate four-minute check proves Auto-Merge remains dormant while readiness is incomplete.

5
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:15,000
Exact-head review approval automatically routes through Fullsend; no human merge command is used.

6
00:01:15,000 --> 00:01:30,000
Trusted preflight validates checks, approval, DCO, scope, threads, mergeability, and bounded patch evidence.

7
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:45,000
The read-only model sandbox has no GitHub token and answers only the bounded semantic question.

8
00:01:45,000 --> 00:02:00,000
Trusted code records a pending receipt, then recollects every mutable fact before mutation.

9
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:15,000
PR #7 receives APPROVE for exact head ae9e2a0; GitHub accepts the exact-head squash merge nine seconds later.

10
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:30,000
The merged receipt closes the loop; production gaps remain explicit, but the authority boundary is proven.
